{"skills":[{"id":"PickPlaceCounterToDrawer-seed7","source_task":"PickPlaceCounterToDrawer","source_seed":7,"official_success":true,"parameters":{"approach":"direct","depth_offset_m":0.0,"pregrasp_distance":0.12,"lift_distance":0.15,"grasp_down_angle":90.0,"release_clearance":0.22,"withdraw_distance":0.2},"source_events":["grasp_hypothesis","pregrasp","descend","close","lift","placement_geometry","leave"],"scope":"Parameters observed in one successful scene; re-localize and replan in a new scene.","source_run":"donor-PickPlaceCounterToDrawer","lesson":"For PickPlaceCounterToDrawer, a direct vertical approach (90-degree descent) with a 0.12m pre-grasp distance and 0.15m lift is effective. The robot should approach the object on the counter, descend vertically to grasp, lift 0.15m, move to the drawer, and release with 0.22m clearance. The 0.2m withdraw distance ensures the arm clears the drawer after release. This sequence works when the object is accessible from above and the drawer is directly below or adjacent to the counter position.","applicability":"Applies to PickPlaceCounterToDrawer tasks where the object is on a counter and the target drawer is accessible. The direct vertical approach requires clear space above the object and sufficient drawer opening width. Re-localize object and drawer positions in new scenes; do not reuse absolute coordinates."},{"id":"PickPlaceCounterToStandMixer-seed7","source_task":"PickPlaceCounterToStandMixer","source_seed":7,"official_success":true,"parameters":{"approach":"side_horizontal","depth_offset_m":0.01,"pregrasp_distance":0.119999,"lift_distance":0.15,"grasp_down_angle":30.0,"release_clearance":0.3,"withdraw_distance":0.05,"side_offset_m":0.250088,"side_clearance":0.07,"staging_rise":0.494612,"approach_height":0.74,"transfer_clearance":0.3},"source_events":["grasp_hypothesis","pregrasp","descend","close","lift","placement_geometry","leave"],"scope":"Parameters observed in one successful scene; re-localize and replan in a new scene.","source_run":"donor-PickPlaceCounterToStandMixer","lesson":"For PickPlaceCounterToStandMixer, a side-horizontal approach with a 30-degree grasp-down angle successfully transfers the object from the counter to the stand mixer. The robot approaches from the side (0.25m offset), descends at an angle to grasp, lifts 0.15m, and places with 0.3m clearance. The staging rise of 0.49m ensures the arm clears obstacles during transit. This approach works when the target is accessible from the side and requires angled grasping.","applicability":"Applies to PickPlace tasks where the source and target are on different surfaces (counter to stand) and the object requires angled grasping. The side approach avoids collisions with surrounding objects."}],"lessons":[{"source_run":"donor-PickPlaceCounterToDrawer","task":"PickPlaceCounterToDrawer","seed":7,"official_success":true,"observed_stop":"success","reflection":{"lesson":"For PickPlaceCounterToDrawer, a direct vertical approach (90-degree descent) with a 0.12m pre-grasp distance and 0.15m lift is effective. The robot should approach the object on the counter, descend vertically to grasp, lift 0.15m, move to the drawer, and release with 0.22m clearance. The 0.2m withdraw distance ensures the arm clears the drawer after release. This sequence works when the object is accessible from above and the drawer is directly below or adjacent to the counter position.","applicability":"Applies to PickPlaceCounterToDrawer tasks where the object is on a counter and the target drawer is accessible. The direct vertical approach requires clear space above the object and sufficient drawer opening width. Re-localize object and drawer positions in new scenes; do not reuse absolute coordinates.","evidence":["Official success with 745 actions","Successful relative motion card with direct approach parameters","Final scene shows robot arm retracted after placement"],"next_attempt":"If this fails in a new scene, try increasing pre-grasp distance to 0.15m for better alignment, or use a slight angled approach (80-85 degrees) if vertical access is obstructed. Ensure release clearance is at least 0.2m to avoid drawer contact.","skill_steps":["Approach object on counter from above with 0.12m pre-grasp distance","Descend vertically (90 degrees) to grasp object","Lift object 0.15m clear of counter","Move to drawer location","Release object with 0.22m clearance above drawer","Withdraw arm 0.2m from drawer"]}},{"source_run":"donor-PickPlaceCounterToStandMixer","task":"PickPlaceCounterToStandMixer","seed":7,"official_success":true,"observed_stop":"success","reflection":{"lesson":"For PickPlaceCounterToStandMixer, a side-horizontal approach with a 30-degree grasp-down angle successfully transfers the object from the counter to the stand mixer. The robot approaches from the side (0.25m offset), descends at an angle to grasp, lifts 0.15m, and places with 0.3m clearance. The staging rise of 0.49m ensures the arm clears obstacles during transit. This approach works when the target is accessible from the side and requires angled grasping.","applicability":"Applies to PickPlace tasks where the source and target are on different surfaces (counter to stand) and the object requires angled grasping. The side approach avoids collisions with surrounding objects.","evidence":["Official success: true","Approach: side_horizontal with 30-degree grasp-down angle","Lift distance: 0.15m, release clearance: 0.3m"],"next_attempt":"Re-localize the object and target in the new scene, then replan the side-horizontal approach with the same grasp-down angle and clearance parameters.","skill_steps":["Approach the object from the side with a 0.25m offset","Descend at a 30-degree angle to grasp the object","Lift the object 0.15m","Move to the stand mixer with 0.3m release clearance","Release the object and withdraw 0.05m"]}},{"source_run":"PickPlaceStoveToCounter-seed7-skill-transfer","task":"PickPlaceStoveToCounter","seed":7,"official_success":false,"observed_stop":"policy_finished_false","reflection":{"lesson":"The robot failed to execute the pick-and-place task because the ready posture did not track, preventing any physical interaction with the tomato. The visual grounding correctly identified the tomato but rejected the grasp due to the projected width exceeding the gripper's capacity. No successful strategy was tested as the robot stopped before attempting a grasp.","applicability":"This failure mode applies to any task where the robot's initial posture tracking is unstable or where the object's dimensions are incompatible with the gripper's projected width in the current view.","evidence":["stop_reason: 'ready posture did not track'","rejected_pairs: 'projected_width_exceeds_gripper'","final_stage: 'ready'"],"next_attempt":"Adjust the camera calibration or gripper width parameters to ensure the projected width of the tomato fits within the gripper's capacity, and verify that the ready posture tracking is stable before initiating the pick action.","skill_steps":[]}},{"source_run":"PickPlaceCounterToSink-baseline","task":"PickPlaceCounterToSink","seed":7,"official_success":false,"observed_stop":"policy_finished_false","reflection":{"lesson":"The direct center-height grasp descended too far into the tall carton; it stopped before closing. Post-run contact diagnosis found palm-object collision.","applicability":"Direct grasps of tall objects with RGB hull height available.","evidence":["No closed event.","The native descent was blocked before the commanded center height.","Post-run simulator contact evidence: palm against task object."],"next_attempt":"Estimate an upper-body grasp from RGB silhouette height, leaving palm clearance.","skill_steps":[]},"review_status":"reviewed_against_native_RGB_public_receipts_and_post_run_contact_diagnostics"},{"source_run":"PickPlaceCounterToSink-height-replay","task":"PickPlaceCounterToSink","seed":7,"official_success":false,"observed_stop":"policy_finished_false","reflection":{"lesson":"Raising the grasp target also raised the pregrasp path; this new path hit the upper cabinet before reaching descent.","applicability":"Objects under an overhead cabinet; height changes must account for the whole arm route.","evidence":["No closed event.","Pregrasp tracking stalled.","Post-run simulator contact evidence: link6 against cabinet shelf."],"next_attempt":"Retain the previously reached approach height while shortening final descent.","skill_steps":[]},"review_status":"reviewed_against_native_RGB_public_receipts_and_post_run_contact_diagnostics"},{"source_run":"PickPlaceCounterToSink-clearance","task":"PickPlaceCounterToSink","seed":7,"official_success":false,"observed_stop":"policy_finished_false","reflection":{"lesson":"The corrected upper-body grasp acquired the carton, but the fixed150 mm lift hit the overhead shelf after about131 mm. Acquisition does not establish full transport or task success.","applicability":"Direct carton grasp in this matched scene; broader transfer untested.","evidence":["Both fingers contacted the source carton after close.","RGB showed the carton lifted clear of the counter.","Lift tracking stopped near the overhead cabinet."],"next_attempt":"Return first to the reached pregrasp height before moving laterally.","skill_steps":["Choose task source in RGB.","Grasp no lower than40 mm below the RGB hull top.","Preserve the original approach height."]},"review_status":"reviewed_against_native_RGB_public_receipts_and_post_run_contact_diagnostics"},{"source_run":"PickPlaceCounterToSink-lowlift","task":"PickPlaceCounterToSink","seed":7,"official_success":false,"observed_stop":"policy_finished_false","reflection":{"lesson":"The carton was acquired and lifted69.4 mm. Four wrist mask selections could not see the sink, and the object slipped during later observation. No transfer or release was executed.","applicability":"Held-object destination observation; only this development scene has been tested.","evidence":["Post